# Performance Optimization Rules

## Performance Budgets

| Metric | Target |
|--------|--------|
| First Contentful Paint (FCP) | < 1.5s |
| Largest Contentful Paint (LCP) | < 2.5s |
| Time to Interactive (TTI) | < 5s |
| Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS) | < 0.1 |
| Initial Page Load | < 3s |
| Lighthouse Score | > 90 |
| Bundle Size (JS) | < 300KB |

## React Compiler (Next.js 16+)

React Compiler is built into Next.js 16+ and provides automatic memoization. This means:

```typescript
// ✅ Don't need manual memoization anymore
function BookingsList({ bookings }) {
  // React Compiler automatically optimizes this
  const sortedBookings = bookings.sort((a, b) => 
    new Date(b.createdAt).getTime() - new Date(a.createdAt).getTime()
  );
  
  return (
    <ul>
      {sortedBookings.map(booking => (
        <BookingCard key={booking.id} booking={booking} />
      ))}
    </ul>
  );
}

// ❌ Avoid unnecessary manual optimization
// Only use useMemo/useCallback if profiling shows issues
function BookingsList({ bookings }) {
  const sortedBookings = useMemo(() => 
    bookings.sort((a, b) => ...),
    [bookings]
  ); // Usually not needed with React Compiler
}
```

## Code Splitting & Lazy Loading

### Component Lazy Loading

```typescript
import { lazy, Suspense } from 'react';
import { LoadingSpinner } from '@/components/shared/LoadingSpinner';

// Lazy load heavy components
const CalendarEditor = lazy(() => import('@/components/calendar/CalendarEditor'));
const RevenueChart = lazy(() => import('@/components/charts/RevenueChart'));
const FormBuilder = lazy(() => import('@/components/forms/FormBuilder'));

export function PropertyPage({ propertyId }) {
  return (
    <div>
      <PropertyHeader propertyId={propertyId} />
      
      <Suspense fallback={<LoadingSpinner />}>
        <CalendarEditor propertyId={propertyId} />
      </Suspense>
      
      <Suspense fallback={<ChartSkeleton />}>
        <RevenueChart propertyId={propertyId} />
      </Suspense>
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Route-Based Code Splitting

```typescript
// Next.js App Router handles this automatically
// Each page.tsx is a separate chunk

// For dynamic imports in pages
const HeavyFeature = dynamic(
  () => import('@/components/features/HeavyFeature'),
  { 
    loading: () => <Skeleton />,
    ssr: false // Disable SSR for client-only components
  }
);
```

